// Title: Sensitive File Recovery From Backup Via Wbadmin.EXE
// ID: 84972c80-251c-4c3a-9079-4f00aad93938
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), frack113
// Date: 2024-05-10
// Tags: attack.credential-access, attack.t1003.003
// Description: Detects the dump of highly sensitive files such as "NTDS.DIT" and "SECURITY" hive.
// Attackers can leverage the "wbadmin" utility in order to dump sensitive files that might contain credential or sensitive information.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where (((process.command_line like "*_ recovery*" and process.command_line like "*_recoveryTarget*" and process.command_line like "*_itemtype:File*") and (process.command_line like "*_\\config\\SAM*" or process.command_line like "*_\\config\\SECURITY*" or process.command_line like "*_\\config\\SYSTEM*" or process.command_line like "*_\\Windows\\NTDS\\NTDS.dit*")) and ((process.executable endswith "\\wbadmin.exe") or (process.pe.original_file_name == "WBADMIN.EXE")))
